                  <perfRes>Harpsichord</perfRes>
               </perfResList>
            </perfMedium>
         </work>
      </workList>
      <revisionDesc>
         <change isodate="2026-10-27" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Corrected 4 encoding errors found in the musical-lint triage: scripts/musical_lint.py flagged notation suspects, an AI model (OpenAI Codex) compared each with the DdT 1903 page image, and the editor spot-checked eight of its findings across the edition before approving the fixes. In m. 142, moved 1 figured-bass figure to the onset at which DdT prints it. In mm. 43, 182, 193, corrected the start or end note of 3 ties to match DdT. Event IDs are retained; all other music is unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-26" resp="#resp.polyakov #resp.camat">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Updated the edition statement and editorial declaration to the corrected status confirmed by the editor on 2026-10-26: the edition statement reads Corrected working edition, still without an edition number until a release includes this work, and the declaration no longer says that work-level review is pending. Publication sign-off remains outside this working edition. The musical text, annotations, facsimile zones and event IDs are unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-26" resp="#resp.camat">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Added an explicit first-page pgHead with the edition title and Dietrich Buxtehude, following the editor's choice to include the composer in exported scores as well as the web viewer. The authority-linked composer and source metadata are retained. All musical events, their IDs, annotations, facsimile references and encoded breaks are unchanged; page counts and MIDI are unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-26" resp="#resp.polyakov #resp.camat">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Aligned the header with the other assembled works: removed the edition number, which is set when a release includes this work; merged the 22 appInfo entries inherited from the page files into one Verovio entry and one mei-friend entry spanning the earliest and latest dates recorded in the page files; and condensed the editorial declaration, whose revision details remain in this history. Removed the inherited metcon=false marker from 96 measures in which every layer fills the meter, as the consistency report confirms. The musical text, annotations, facsimile zones and event IDs are unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-26" resp="#resp.camat">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Completed the import cleanup specified by CAMAT's mei_combine_pages notebook: removed the remaining 93 accid.ges attributes with strip_accid_ges_text, matching prepare_pages_for_combine(strip_accid_ges=True). The already removed ppq and dur.ppq attributes remain absent. Written accid attributes, accid elements, key signatures, pitch names, octaves, durations, ties, voices and event IDs are retained. This removes inherited gestural accidental overrides; no playback-specific accidentals have been added.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-26" resp="#resp.camat">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Corrected six stem directions in five beamed groups after direct comparison with DdT: the lower keyboard beams in measures 13, 30 and 72 have downward stems, the upper keyboard beam in measure 29 has upward stems (printed p. 80), and the opening violin beam in measure 53 has downward stems throughout (p. 82; m. 72 on p. 83). Changed u4ufpp6, r1qgvsn7k, o14lgp34, p1srz5h5 and i6ze to down, and angsnyxxth to up. All pitches, note values, voice membership, beam grouping, ties and event IDs are retained. This corrects the mixed-stem overrides responsible for five Verovio beam-placement warnings.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 2, staff 4, normalized the second D4-F4-B-flat4 chord h1oci7l53 to the printed dotted quarter and upward stem, as confirmed by Egor Polyakov against DdT p. 79. Removed individual duration, dot and stem overrides from tones la0vt8w, z144051hs and a17oyd6zl: the B-flat4 duplicated the parent duration and dot, while F4 and D4 incorrectly carried sixteenth-note durations and downward stems. All tones now inherit the chord's dotted-quarter duration and upward stem. Every layer fills 6/8; removed the inherited metcon=false marker from this reviewed full measure. Pitches, written accidentals, event IDs and all other music are retained.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 30, staff 4, layer 1, removed stale gestural flat accid.ges=f from final A4 eighth b1eoe3cf while retaining its printed natural abxgtxz2, as confirmed by Egor Polyakov against DdT p. 80 and the aligned final A3 natural in the gamba. The keyboard note now sounds A-natural4 rather than A-flat4. The written natural, pitch name, octave, event IDs, durations and all other musical events are retained.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Removed redundant staff attributes from inline clefs c1dstmp1 (m. 13), cbr4882 (m. 14), ciohtfd1 (m. 28), ccmr4md1 (m. 55), clm5bxd and cgermfe1 (m. 66). Each explicitly named the same staff as its containing staff element. The clefs inherit that staff; all clef shapes, lines, IDs, positions and every other musical event are retained. This removes six Verovio cross-staff warnings without changing the printed clef changes.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 199, staff 5, removed extra hidden eighth-note space gkvlnmy from the final beam b1ivd5j2, as confirmed by Egor Polyakov against DdT p. 89. The closing four eighth notes are consecutive as printed; every layer now fills 6/4. Removed the inherited metcon=false marker from this reviewed full measure. All printed notes and durations, their beaming, ties and remaining event IDs are retained.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 193, staff 5, moved final down-stem G2 quarter v17yxj8m from layer 2 into layer 1, replacing its final hidden quarter-note space ojere, as confirmed by Egor Polyakov against DdT p. 89. G2 now falls on beat 6 in the lower voice while the upper G3 half spans beats 5-6. Every layer fills 6/4; removed the inherited metcon=false marker from this reviewed full measure. The moved note's ID, pitch, written duration and stem, all other printed notes, and existing ties are retained.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 181, staff 5, restored the printed dot on opening F3 half note qn70ao5, as confirmed by Egor Polyakov against DdT p. 88. The dotted half, quarter rest and four eighth notes total the active 6/4 meter. Every layer now fills 6/4; removed the inherited metcon=false marker from this reviewed full measure. The note's pitch, stem and ID, all other note values and events, and the upper keyboard tie into measure 182 are retained.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Completed the two printed keyboard ties across the page break at measures 167-168, as confirmed by Egor Polyakov against DdT pp. 87-88. Explicit tie op2.01.m167.g5-tie connects G5 u1bkmptp to jb75wgk above the staff; op2.01.m167.g4-tie connects G4 a7pyult to tessnfe below the staff. Removed the isolated initial tie attribute from a7pyult and terminal tie attribute from jb75wgk. The explicit endpoints replace the two incomplete attribute-based ties and prevent the inferred G4 tie from seeking a terminal note in measure 169. All note pitches, durations, voice membership, existing IDs and other ties are retained.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 166, staff 4, layer 3, shortened final hidden space i1uo67zz from a dotted whole to a dotted half, as agreed after comparison with DdT p. 87. The initial quarter-note space, B-flat4 quarter, A4 quarter and final dotted-half space now total 6/4. All seven layers fill the active meter; removed the inherited metcon=false marker from this reviewed full measure. Printed notes, their durations, ties and existing event IDs are retained.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 163, staff 4, layer 1, supplied a dot on opening A-flat4 quarter g102zyi8, as confirmed by Egor Polyakov after comparison with DdT p. 87. The dotted quarter restores 6/4 and places C5 on beat 3 with the lower-voice F4 eighth. Annotation editorial.op2.01.m163.aflat4-dot documents the apparent printed undotted quarter, encoded replacement and conjectural rhythmic rationale. Every layer fills the active meter. The note ID, pitch, written accidental and stem, all other musical events and the lower F4 tie are retained.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 153, staff 4, layer 2, removed the dot from final hidden half-note space jdfijdge, as agreed after comparison with DdT p. 87. The tied A3 quarter is followed by a hidden half-note space, totaling the active 3/4 meter. Every layer now fills 3/4. All printed notes and durations, the A3 tie and existing event IDs are retained.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 147, applied three repairs confirmed by Egor Polyakov against DdT p. 86: removed the extra trailing hidden sixteenth-note space ae7eesv from staff 3; restored missing D4 as op2.01.m147.s4.d4 in the opening D4-G4-B-flat4 dotted-quarter keyboard chord pk0z978; and completed staff 4, layer 2 with hidden half-note space op2.01.m147.s4.l2.space after the D4-F-sharp4 eighth. Every layer now fills 4/4; removed the inherited metcon=false marker. All other printed notes and durations, ties, fermatas, the final double barline and remaining event IDs are retained.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 143, staff 2, removed extra trailing hidden quarter-note space d445jze after Egor Polyakov confirmed the complete gamba line in DdT p. 86. The eight sixteenths, D3 quarter, eighth rest and final B-flat2 eighth already fill 4/4. Every layer now fills the active meter; removed the inherited metcon=false marker from this reviewed full measure. All printed notes and rests, their durations, ties and remaining IDs are retained.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 142, staff 5, layer 2, shortened final hidden space x9wnm0p from a half note to a dotted quarter after the editor confirmed the D4 voice in DdT p. 86. The layer now comprises a quarter-note space, D4 quarter, D4 eighth and dotted-quarter space, totaling 4/4. Every layer fills the active meter; removed the inherited metcon=false marker from this reviewed full measure. All printed notes, written note durations, ties and existing IDs are retained.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 135, staff 5, restored the final printed eighth rest as op2.01.m135.s5.rest after A3 oi84, following Egor Polyakov's confirmation against DdT p. 86. The keyboard bass now contains four eighth notes alternating with four eighth rests and fills 4/4, matching the figured continuo's rhythmic sequence. All existing note values, pitches, cross-staff chord tones, ties and IDs are retained.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 128, staff 5, restored the printed dot on opening B-flat2 eighth a1d1aczt after Egor Polyakov confirmed DdT p. 85. The first pair is now a dotted eighth followed by a sixteenth and the voice fills 4/4. The note's pitch, duration base, stem direction and ID, all beaming and every other musical event are retained.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 125, staff 5, layer 2, added hidden quarter-note space op2.01.m125.s5.l2.space after the printed B-flat2-A2-D2 quarters, as agreed by the editor after comparison with DdT p. 85. The printed final quarter rest is already represented in layer 1; the space completes layer 2 to 4/4 without adding a duplicate visible rest. All existing notes, durations, IDs and ties are retained. At the editor's request, widened the Uppsala/STIMU excerpt for measure 114 to show the complete printed bar corresponding to DdT measures 113–114, including both barlines. Updated its annotation caption, documentation and crop provenance; the E4 dotted-whole reading is unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 114, staff 2, added a dot to E4 whole note wmjri1r, following Egor Polyakov's proposal and direct comparison with the Uppsala Op. II print through STIMU 1991: Viola da Gamba, Sonata I, Grave, printed p. 4, fifth staff, scan-0027, left-hand page. The historical print has a dotted whole where DdT p. 85 has an undotted whole. Added source-supported annotation editorial.op2.01.m114.e4-dot, witness and carrier descriptions, and a linked measure-level facsimile excerpt with crop provenance. Every layer now fills 3/2; removed the inherited metcon=false marker. All other musical events and existing IDs are retained. This is a selected comparison, not a complete historical-print collation or publication sign-off.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Moved continuo G3-G3 tie i1htfxj5 from measure 104 into its starting measure 103, as agreed by the editor after comparison with DdT p. 84. Its endpoints h15qag3x and uffs85n, tie attributes, notes and durations are unchanged. This encoding-location repair retains the printed tie and removes Verovio's destination-measure warning.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 102, staff 1, added the missing printed dot to E5 whole note h1b6xppn after Egor Polyakov confirmed the DdT p. 84 facsimile. The violin now has a dotted whole and every layer fills 3/2; removed the inherited metcon=false marker from this reviewed full measure. The note's pitch, duration base and ID, and all other musical events are retained.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 90, staff 4, layer 2, restored the late F4 as an eighth on the final eighth-note subdivision, following Egor Polyakov's proposed and confirmed reading of DdT p. 84. Added hidden half-note space op2.01.m090.s4.l2.space after the earlier D4 quarter and new F4 op2.01.m090.s4.l2.f4. Annotation editorial.op2.01.m090.f4 records the apparent printed quarter form, conjectural replacement and rhythmic rationale. All layers now fill 4/4; removed the inherited metcon=false marker. All pre-existing notes and their attributes, ties and event IDs are retained.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 90, staff 5, removed extra trailing hidden quarter-note space potmuzq after the editor confirmed the keyboard bass in DdT p. 84. The printed bass line already fills 4/4 and matches the figured continuo's rhythmic sequence. All sounding notes, written note durations, ties and remaining event IDs are retained.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 89, staff 4, layer 2, added hidden half-note space op2.01.m089.s4.l2.space after the final E4 sixteenth, as agreed after the editor's comparison with DdT p. 84. The printed lower voice occupies the first two beats; the space completes the remaining two beats. Every layer now fills 4/4; removed the inherited metcon=false marker from this reviewed full measure. All printed notes, written durations, ties and existing event IDs are retained.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 84, staff 2, inserted missing G2 sixteenth op2.01.m084.s2.g2 between the first A2 and F2 in beam adq94v3 after the editor confirmed the DdT p. 83 reading. The closing groups after the bass-clef change are F2-G2 and A2-G2-F2-A2, all sixteenths. Every layer now fills 4/4. The clef change, all existing note IDs and readings, and all other musical events are retained.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 80, staff 2, restored the editor-confirmed closing sixteenths C4-B-flat3-A-flat3-B-flat3-C4-A-flat3 from DdT p. 83. Inserted the missing leading C4 as op2.01.m080.s2.c4, corrected existing B-flat3 e1iqkviu from a quarter to a sixteenth, and beamed that first pair as printed. The following four sixteenths retain their IDs and readings. Every layer now fills 4/4; removed the inherited metcon=false marker from this reviewed full measure. All other musical events are unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 79, staff 4, moved closing eighth-note chords urznz and urznzax with their beam q14n3uqu into layer 1 after the editor confirmed the printed upper voice quarter-quarter-eighth-eighth-eighth-eighth in DdT p. 83. Moved existing hidden space d145850i to the end of layer 2 and changed it from an eighth to a quarter, completing that partial lower voice. All layers now fill 4/4. Every existing event ID, pitch, written note duration and tie is retained; other measures are unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 74, staff 2, corrected final rest r1pzb1qv from a sixteenth to a quarter after the editor confirmed the quarter rest in DdT p. 83. The gamba voice now fills 4/4. The rest ID, preceding bass-clef change and all sounding notes are retained; all other musical events are unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 68, staff 4, layer 2, removed the extra hidden 32nd-note space w1s0fh9y3 after the editor confirmed the DdT p. 82 reading. Retained hidden eighth space w10fh9y3 and the final F4 eighth s9rredd, which now begins on the last eighth of the 4/4 bar. Every layer fills common time; removed the inherited metcon=false marker from this reviewed full measure. Pitches, written note durations and all other musical events are unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measures 57-58, staves 3-5, removed dur=2 from the six full-measure rests after the editor confirmed the rests printed in DdT p. 82. The continuo and both keyboard staves now inherit the active 4/4 measure duration. All rest IDs and all other musical events are retained; every layer in both measures fills common time.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measures 54-55, staff 2, removed dur=2 from full-measure rests phx8ds6 and phx8sds6 after the editor confirmed the full-bar rests printed in DdT p. 82. The mRest elements now inherit the active common-time measure duration. All layers fill 4/4; removed the inherited metcon=false marker from measure 55. Rest IDs, the following gamba clef change, and all other musical events are retained.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 41, staff 4, layer 1, removed the extra trailing hidden eighth-note space t8o5szo after the editor confirmed the printed quarter-eighth-eighth-quarter rhythm against DdT p. 81. The sounding voice already fills 6/8; the space made it overfull. Notes, written note durations, ties and all other musical events are unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 35, staff 4, encoded the editor-confirmed final D4-F4-B-flat4 chord as a dotted quarter by placing dots=1 on chord v1ekdacfo. Removed the redundant dur=4 and dots=1 attributes from its three tones so that they inherit the chord duration. The rhythm now fills 6/8: eighth rest, two eighth chords, dotted-quarter chord. Pitches, printed dots and all existing event IDs are retained; other musical events are unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 18, staff 4, layer 1, added hidden dotted-quarter space op2.01.m018.s4.l1.space after the printed D4-F4 dotted-quarter chord, as agreed with the editor after comparison with DdT p. 80. This completes the partial lower voice to 6/8 while retaining all printed notes, durations, voice membership and existing event IDs.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 14, staff 4, layer 2, removed the extra dot from hidden eighth-note space j69fzja after the editor confirmed the correction against DdT p. 80. The printed lower voice has three eighths and a quarter, followed by one eighth of hidden padding; the layer now fills 6/8. All sounding notes, written note durations and existing event IDs are unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 12, staff 4, restored the editor-confirmed printed upper-voice rhythm eighth-eighth-eighth-quarter-eighth. Changed the second A4 b1ukus1t to an eighth and moved the three closing chords from layer 2 into layer 1, retaining their IDs and pitches. Removed the eleven redundant or conflicting chord-tone duration attributes so that the tones inherit their chord durations. The lower C4-F4 eighths remain in layer 2, followed by a hidden half-note space to complete 6/8. All six layers now fill the full measure; removed its inherited metcon=false marker. All existing musical event IDs and all other measures are unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 4, corrected two OMR duration errors after the editor confirmed the DdT p. 79 readings: removed the extra dot from the gamba opening B-flat3 eighth note hrrmcev and inserted the missing continuo D3 sixteenth op2.01.m004.s3.d3 before the final B-flat2. The latter restores the printed second group D3-C3-B-flat2-C3-D3-B-flat2, also present in the keyboard lower staff. All six layers now fill 6/8; removed the inherited metcon=false marker from this reviewed full measure. Existing event IDs and all other musical events are unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 112, staff 5, supplied the missing pitch name b on note rsjlxn6 after the editor confirmed the B-flat2 dotted whole note printed on DdT p. 85. The existing octave, duration, augmentation dot and event ID are retained; the two-flat key signature supplies the flat. All other musical events are unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Applied the same normalize_single_layer_numbers behavior enabled in CAMAT's mei_combine_pages.ipynb: renumbered nineteen single layers on staff 5 to 1. Separately corrected the duplicate layer number at measure 32, staff 4: retained the upper up-stem voice r1jol63s as layer 1 and numbered the lower down-stem voice x1e278fi as layer 2, as agreed with the editor and consistent with neighboring measures. Notes, written durations, voice membership, event IDs and references are unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measure 203, restored one upright fermata above the final event on each of the five staves, as the editor confirmed in DdT printed p. 89. Corrected the staff assignments of l1v57l5j, w11fpfoz and p1kkptu8; attached fypu3qv to the final upper keyboard chord a1nu692 on staff 4; made the upper placement of fe5fgbd explicit; and removed the duplicate violin fermata f0qxavk2. Notes, chords, written durations and all other musical events are unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>At measures 188-189, removed the stale duplicate keyboard tie dsg3rat after the editor confirmed a single B4-B4 tie in DdT printed p. 89. Retained t6rbhzk1 and its existing endpoints y1tcezp and z1a7veqx. The valid violin tie and all other musical events are unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Removed the stale tie u19kbugw at measure 95 after the editor confirmed that DdT printed p. 84 has no tie there. Its two D4 endpoints had already been deleted during page correction; the upper keyboard staff remains empty and the lower-staff chord is retained. All notes, written durations and remaining event IDs are unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>After the editor confirmed a single B4-B4 tie in DdT at measures 7-8, removed the stale duplicate tie tv1yey9 and retained taewfxc with its existing endpoints. Restored the printed opening instrument labels Violino., Viola da gamba. and Cembalo., a bracket enclosing staves 1-3 and the existing keyboard brace enclosing staves 4-5. Grouping is retained in all eleven page-start staff definitions. No slur was added; pitches, written durations and remaining event IDs are unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Removed 55 ppq and 6478 dur.ppq attributes left from MusicXML conversion, following the PPQ cleanup in CAMAT's mei_combine_pages.ipynb and the other 16 assembled scores. Written durations, dots, tuplets, pitches, accidentals, event IDs and references are unchanged. This removes the obsolete PPQ mismatch findings; remaining musical-duration warnings still require source review.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Assembled 11 proofread page files into a 203-measure working score. Preserved musical readings, page-specific notation context, software history and the recovered final bar. Added work, source, responsibility and license metadata, linked 11 facsimile surfaces, renumbered measures and zones, made colliding IDs unique and changed eight within-page page breaks to system breaks. Full work-level consistency review remains pending; this file was not part of the 0.9.0 pre-release.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
      </revisionDesc>
