                     <annot xml:id="editorial.op2.01.m090.f4" type="editorial" label="conjectural-emendation" plist="#op2.01.m090.s4.l2.f4" resp="#resp.polyakov">
                        <p><ref target="#src.ddt1903">DdT 1903</ref>, printed p. 84 (BSB image 94), measure 90, keyboard upper staff, lower voice: the late down-stem F4 appears as a quarter note. It is encoded here conjecturally as an eighth on the final eighth-note subdivision of the 4/4 measure (beat 4.5), as proposed and approved by Egor Polyakov on 2026-10-25 after inspecting the facsimile. At this onset a quarter would extend an eighth beyond the barline; the eighth ends with the upper voice and bass. A hidden half-note space after the earlier D4 quarter places F4 at that onset. The encoded layer totals an eighth-note space, D4 quarter, half-note space and F4 eighth = 4/4. Only DdT was consulted; no historical-witness support is claimed for the replacement duration.</p>
                     </annot>
