                     <tie xml:id="tvpzflb" endid="#wzk29ar" staff="4" startid="#jdfker"/>
                     <annot xml:id="editorial.op2.01.m163.aflat4-dot" type="editorial" label="conjectural-emendation" plist="#g102zyi8" resp="#resp.polyakov">
                        <p><ref target="#src.ddt1903">DdT 1903</ref>, printed p. 87 (BSB image 97), measure 163, keyboard upper staff, upper voice: the opening A-flat4 appears as an undotted quarter. A dot is supplied conjecturally, encoding a dotted quarter, as confirmed by Egor Polyakov on 2026-10-25. The resulting rhythm is dotted quarter, eighth, quarter, dotted quarter, eighth, quarter, totaling twelve eighth notes (= 6/4); the undotted opening gives only eleven eighths. The dot places the following B-flat4 eighth on beat 2.5 and C5 quarter on beat 3, aligned with the lower voice's F4 eighth after its tied F4 half note. This is a conjectural emendation of DdT's keyboard realization. Only DdT was consulted for this decision; no historical-witness support is claimed.</p>
                     </annot>
                  </measure>
